        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "20f346ce-706f-5162-8174-5961b161e0d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnston Forbes-Robertson, Prince Hamlet, Gertrude Elliott, Claudius, King Hamlet, Maxine Elliott\n- Roles: Prince of Denmark, actor, stage actress, Lady Forbes-Robertson\n- Topics: Victorian-era theatre, Shakespearean acting, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Prince Hamlet is the Prince of Denmark, the son of King Hamlet, and the nephew of Claudius, who has usurped the Danish throne.\n- Gertrude Elliott was born on December 14, 1874, and she was an American stage actress.\n- Gertrude Elliott belonged to an extended family of theatre professionals that included her husband Johnston Forbes-Robertson and her sister Maxine Elliott.\n- Johnston Forbes-Robertson was regarded as the finest Hamlet of the Victorian era and as one of the finest actors of his time.\n- Johnston Forbes-Robertson disliked acting and believed throughout his life that he was temperamentally unsuited to the profession.\n- Gertrude Elliott later held the title Lady Forbes-Robertson.\n- Gertrude Elliott died on December 24, 1950.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
